  "body": "**Provider-native web search**\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Web search now uses your model provider's own server-side search (Anthropic and OpenAI) by default instead of scraping from your machine, shown as regular web search rows live and on resume (thanks @johnnyfish)\n\n### Improvements\n\n- Set websearch.prefer_native = false or JCODE_WEBSEARCH_PREFER_NATIVE=0 to keep using local search engines\n- Provider-side search follows each session's allowed and disabled tool policy\n- SDK apps that register their own websearch tool keep it instead of having it replaced by provider search\n- Installing a skill mid-session no longer invalidates the prompt cache, so the next turn stays fast and cheap\n- When switching providers, earlier native search results are summarized clearly so the model does not retract correct answers\n\n### Fixes\n\n- OpenAI login validation no longer hangs when the account hits a usage limit\n- Retrying a turn no longer leaves web search rows from the aborted attempt\n- Interrupted Anthropic turns that used native search no longer risk a request error on the next message\n\n**Full changelog**: https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/compare/v0.89.3...v0.90.0\n\n<!-- jcode-platform-availability:start -->\n## Platform availability\n\n- Linux x86_64: available\n- Linux aarch64: available\n- macOS Apple Silicon: available\n- macOS Intel: available\n- Windows x86_64: available\n- Windows ARM64: available\n- FreeBSD x86_64: available\n<!-- jcode-platform-availability:end -->\n\n<!-- jcode-discord-announced:v0.90.0 -->\n",
